{"term":"bruise","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:02074521bf876ef1a0","definition":"To strike (a person), originally with something flat or heavy, but now specifically in such a way as to discolour the skin without breaking it; to contuse.","example":"It is as I have spoken: the testing first, next the bruising, and in the last bout the breaking and killing.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bruisability","bruisable","bruisedness","bruiser","bruise up","bruising","unbruised"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bruise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2c0cb7452fbdb7af8a","definition":"To damage the skin of (fruit or vegetables), in an analogous way.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bruisability","bruisable","bruisedness","bruiser","bruise up","bruising","unbruised"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bruise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5d15d79838bfb16e7b","definition":"Of fruit or vegetables, to gain bruises through being handled roughly.","example":"Bananas bruise easily.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["bruisability","bruisable","bruisedness","bruiser","bruise up","bruising","unbruised"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bruise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:74c75670d104d9c248","definition":"To become bruised.","example":"I bruise easily.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["bruisability","bruisable","bruis